<title>CHINA: China February oil products import, export totals. [CORRECTED 11:55 GMT]</title>
<headline>China February oil products import, export totals. [CORRECTED 11:55 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's imports and exports of</p>
<p>oil products as reported in official customs figures (percentage</p>
<p>change is for Jan-Feb 1997 period compared with last year):</p>
<p>(Corrects month of first column in tables to February from January.)</p>
<p>		 FEBRUARY IMPORTS  JAN-FEB IMPORTS  VS PVS YEAR</p>
<p> Gasoline	    9,298	   10,858	 - 8.0 PERCENT</p>
<p> Jet fuel		  0		  0.015   -99.0</p>
<p> Naphtha	    12,656	   12,660	 -86.0</p>
<p> Kerosene	  122,804	  155,779    +4,420.0</p>
<p>Light diesel</p>
<p> fuel		817,737	1,269,512	 +97.0</p>
<p>Heavy diesel</p>
<p> fuel			0.36	    14	 -99.0</p>
<p>Liquefied natural</p>
<p> gas		  21,834	   56,481  +102,093.0</p>
<p> Propane	    12,308	   25,236	 -84.0</p>
<p>(Note: all figures in tonnes)</p>
<p>		FEBRUARY EXPORTS  JAN-FEB EXPORTS  VS PVS YEAR</p>
<p> Gasoline	  166,407	240,781	  +615.0 PERCENT</p>
<p> Jet fuel	    2,000	  2,000	     -</p>
<p> Naphtha	    18,394	 18,394	     -</p>
<p> Kerosene	   52,536	106,283	   +19.0</p>
<p>Light diesel</p>
<p> fuel		 48,579	124,975	   -47.0</p>
<p>Heavy diesel</p>
<p> fuel			0		0	  -100.0</p>
<p>Liquefied natural</p>
<p> gas			 0		0	  -100.0</p>
<p> Propane		   0	    900	   -94.0</p>
<p>(Note: all figures in tonnes)</p>
</text>
